---
id: org.dxos.spec.changelog
name: DSL.Changelog
version: 1.0
extends:
  - org.dxos.spec.core
---

The changelog dialect. Adds a `## Changelog` section to a spec: an append-only log of the
authoritative decisions that shaped it, each one attributed to the person or the agent that made
it. The body of a spec says what is true now; the changelog says who decided it, when, and why.

A spec is written by people and agents together, and the two carry different authority. A person
can set direction; an agent decides within the latitude a person gave it. The log keeps the two
apart by construction — every entry names exactly one decider, typed as `user:` or `agent:` — so
"which parts of this spec did a human choose?" is a filter, not an archaeology project.

## Extensions

| Term       | URI                          |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |

## Actors

Every actor reference carries one of two prefixes. The prefix is the point of the dialect: the
linter rejects a `by:` without one.

| Form              | Who                                                   | Example                       |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `user:<handle>`   | A person, by GitHub username or email.                | `user:alice`, `user:a@b.org` |
| `agent:<name>`    | An agent, by harness or product name — never a model. | `agent:claude-code`           |

Name an agent by what ran it (`agent:claude-code`, `agent:composer-assistant`), not by the model
that served it: models change mid-session and the name must stay stable across the log.

## Rules

1. **One decision per entry, one decider per decision.** A decision two people made together is
   recorded as the one who made the call; the other goes in prose.
2. **The decider is who chose, not who typed.** An agent that writes down a choice a person stated
   records `by: user:<them>` and links where they said it in `source:`. An agent records
   `by: agent:<name>` only for a choice it made itself.
3. **An agent decision names its principal.** `for:` is the person whose instruction the agent was
   acting under. It is required on `agent:` entries and forbidden on `user:` entries.
4. **Ratification is a separate fact.** When a person later endorses an agent decision, add
   `ratified-by: user:<them>` to that entry; do not rewrite `by:`. This is the only edit an
   existing entry admits.
5. **Append-only.** Never delete or reword a past entry. To reverse or refine one, append a new
   entry with `supersedes: D-n`. The superseded entry stays — it is the trace.
6. **Authoritative only.** Log decisions that changed what the spec requires: a type, a
   requirement, a boundary, a rejected alternative that will be proposed again. Do not log edits,
   typo fixes, or reformatting — git has those.
7. **Identifiers are monotonic.** `D-1`, `D-2`, … in the order appended. Never reuse or renumber.
8. **Newest last.** The section reads as a timeline.

## Definitions

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One authoritative decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose
    is the decision itself, stated as what is now true ("Bounds are derived, never stored."), not
    as the change that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    ratified-by?: UserRef       # a person who later endorsed an agent decision
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains, e.g. [Scene, F-2.1]
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the constraint or evidence that forced the choice
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```

## Example

```mdl
decision D-1: Bounds are derived from content, never stored.
  date: 2026-10-02
  by: user:alice
  affects: [Scene]
  why: Stored bounds drift from the content whenever a node moves outside an edit path.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/<n>
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Bounds grow to the major grid, not the minor one.
  date: 2026-10-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:alice
  affects: [Scene, F-2.1]
  why: Growing to the minor grid re-lays the canvas on every drag step.
  rejected:
    - Fixed padding: clips large nodes at the edge.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Bounds grow to the minor grid while dragging and snap to the major grid on drop.
  date: 2026-10-05
  by: user:alice
  supersedes: D-2
  why: The major grid felt laggy in review; snapping on drop keeps layout stable.
```
